From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:22:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] eigen_common_wrapper.h: Ignore GCC's C++20 implicit this
 capture deprecation

ONNX Runtime builds as C++20. Eigen releases up to 3.4.x capture 'this'
implicitly through '[=]' in the unsupported Tensor module, which GCC
diagnoses under -Wdeprecated:

  unsupported/Eigen/CXX11/src/Tensor/TensorDeviceThreadPool.h:210:19:
  error: implicit capture of 'this' via '[=]' is deprecated in C++20
  [-Werror=deprecated]

The wrapper already ignores the clang equivalent
(-Wdeprecated-this-capture), which GCC does not have. Ignore
-Wdeprecated for GCC around the Eigen include as well, so that building
against an installed Eigen 3.4.x works with -Werror.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
---
 include/onnxruntime/core/common/eigen_common_wrapper.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/onnxruntime/core/common/eigen_common_wrapper.h b/include/onnxruntime/core/common/eigen_common_wrapper.h
index 19efa7b..13dccdf 100644
--- a/include/onnxruntime/core/common/eigen_common_wrapper.h
+++ b/include/onnxruntime/core/common/eigen_common_wrapper.h
@@ -55,6 +55,14 @@
 #pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wdeprecated-this-capture"
 #endif
 
+// GCC reports the same deprecation under -Wdeprecated when building as C++20
+// against an Eigen release that predates the fix (e.g. 3.4.x):
+// unsupported/Eigen/CXX11/src/Tensor/TensorDeviceThreadPool.h:210:19:
+// error: implicit capture of 'this' via '[=]' is deprecated in C++20 [-Werror=deprecated]
+#if !defined(__clang__)
+#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wdeprecated"
+#endif
+
 #elif defined(_MSC_VER)
 // build\windows\debug\external\eigen3\unsupported\eigen\cxx11\src/Tensor/Tensor.h(76):
 // warning C4554: '&': check operator precedence for possible error; use parentheses to clarify precedence
